Subject: Re: Acme POC - post-call recap and next steps (technical checklist)

Hi John / team — looking forward to the kickoff. Quick technical checklist and a small Node example you can try locally before the call: 

Checklist (what we need from Acme before kickoff):
- API allowlist: add redwood-poc@acme.com to your firewall for callback tests (if you want Redwood to call your enrichment endpoint).
- Test service endpoint for enrichment: URL + auth method (Bearer token preferred).
- Sample dataset: share 40 evaluation cases (zip) and a small live sample (10 records) for latency testing.

Minimal Node streaming + function-schema example (pseudo-code):

const { RedwoodClient } = require('redwood-sdk');
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });

const stream = await client.stream('/v1/stream', {
  model: 'redwood-llama-13b',
  input: 'Extract entities from this CRM note...',
  stream: true,
  functions: [{ name: 'enrich', schema: { type: 'object', properties: { id: { type: 'string' } } } }]
});

for await (const chunk of stream) {
  if (chunk.type === 'tool_call') {
    // Redwood suggests calling your enrichment service
    const result = await callAcmeEnrichment(chunk.args);
    await client.toolResponse(chunk.call_id, result);
  } else if (chunk.type === 'token') {
    process.stdout.write(chunk.text);
  }
}

Notes:
- We will instrument cold vs warm latencies and include both in the POC dashboard.
- Log retention for POC requests: by default logs/trace metadata retained for 30 days; we can increase retention for debugging if you need it (requires a short addendum).

I'll attach the SDK quickstart and a small Postman collection in the kickoff calendar invite. See you Mon at 10am PT.

